{
 "cells": [
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "# Fisher matrix calculations for Continuous Gravitational Wave\n\nHere the source is considered to be a non-axisymmetric isolated neutron star.\n\nThis notebook contains the derivatives and the Fisher matrix calculations.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {},
   "executionSummary": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## CW model\n\nFor the waveform model, we use the $2f$ component of the GW signal.\n\nThe reference for the waveform model is [Jaranowski et al. 1998](https://arxiv.org/pdf/gr-qc/9804014).",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {},
   "executionSummary": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "$$h(t) = \\sum_{i=1}^{4} A_{2i}\\,h_{2i}(t),\\qquad\nh_{21} = a(t)\\cos\\Phi,\\ \\ h_{22} = b(t)\\cos\\Phi,\\ \\ h_{23} = a(t)\\sin\\Phi,\\ \\ h_{24} = b(t)\\sin\\Phi,$$\n\n$$\\Phi(t) = 2\\pi\\left(f t + \\tfrac12\\dot f t^2\\right) + \\frac{2\\pi}{c}\\,(\\vec n\\cdot\\vec r)(t)\\,\\left(f+\\dot f t\\right).$$\n\n- $f,\\dot f$ are the frequency and spindown **of the 2f signal**.\n- $a(t)$, $b(t)$ are the antenna pattern functions.\n- $\\vec n$ is the unit vector pointing to the source, $\\vec r$ is the detector position vector in the SSB frame.\n- $\\vec n\\cdot\\vec r$ is the detector position projected on the source direction (from your ephemeris + detector location), in metres.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {},
   "executionSummary": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "ClearAll[\"Global`*\"];\n\nampPars   = {h0, iota, psi, phi0};\nphasePars = {f, fdot, alpha, delta};\npars      = {h0, f, fdot, alpha, delta, iota, psi, phi0};\n\n(* modulation functions and Doppler term (kept abstract) *)\naF  = a[alpha, delta, t];\nbF  = b[alpha, delta, t];\nnrF = nr[alpha, delta, t];\n\n(* amplitudes, wobble angle theta = Pi/2, arm angle zeta = Pi/2 *)\nAmp = h0 {\n    1/2 (1 + Cos[iota]^2) Cos[2 psi] Cos[phi0] - Cos[iota] Sin[2 psi] Sin[phi0],\n    1/2 (1 + Cos[iota]^2) Sin[2 psi] Cos[phi0] + Cos[iota] Cos[2 psi] Sin[phi0],\n   -1/2 (1 + Cos[iota]^2) Cos[2 psi] Sin[phi0] - Cos[iota] Sin[2 psi] Cos[phi0],\n   -1/2 (1 + Cos[iota]^2) Sin[2 psi] Sin[phi0] + Cos[iota] Cos[2 psi] Cos[phi0]};\n\n(* phase *)\nPhi = 2 Pi (f t + fdot t^2/2) + (2 Pi/c) nrF (f + fdot t);\n\n(* cw modes h21, h22, h23, h24 *)\nmodes = {aF Cos[Phi], bF Cos[Phi], aF Sin[Phi], bF Sin[Phi]};\n\nh = Amp . modes;",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {},
   "executionSummary": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Notation for the output\n\nDisplay only (`TraditionalForm`); the expressions keep their plain names, so `CForm` is unaffected.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {},
   "executionSummary": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "MakeBoxes[h0, TraditionalForm]     := SubscriptBox[\"h\", \"0\"];\nMakeBoxes[iota, TraditionalForm]   := \"\\[Iota]\";\nMakeBoxes[psi, TraditionalForm]    := \"\\[Psi]\";\nMakeBoxes[phi0, TraditionalForm]   := SubscriptBox[\"\\[Phi]\", \"0\"];\nMakeBoxes[fdot, TraditionalForm]   := OverscriptBox[\"f\", \".\"];\nMakeBoxes[alpha, TraditionalForm]  := \"\\[Alpha]\";\nMakeBoxes[delta, TraditionalForm]  := \"\\[Delta]\";\nMakeBoxes[lambda, TraditionalForm] := \"\\[Lambda]\";\nMakeBoxes[gam, TraditionalForm]    := \"\\[Gamma]\";\nMakeBoxes[phir, TraditionalForm]   := SubscriptBox[\"\\[Phi]\", \"r\"];\nMakeBoxes[OmegaR, TraditionalForm] := SubscriptBox[\"\\[CapitalOmega]\", \"r\"];\nMakeBoxes[rx, TraditionalForm]     := SubscriptBox[\"r\", \"x\"];\nMakeBoxes[ry, TraditionalForm]     := SubscriptBox[\"r\", \"y\"];\nMakeBoxes[rz, TraditionalForm]     := SubscriptBox[\"r\", \"z\"];\n\nnrBox = RowBox[{OverscriptBox[\"n\", \"\\[RightVector]\"], \"\\[CenterDot]\", OverscriptBox[\"r\", \"\\[RightVector]\"]}];\nMakeBoxes[nr, TraditionalForm]     := nrBox;\nMakeBoxes[cosPhi, TraditionalForm] := RowBox[{\"cos\", \"\\[ThinSpace]\", \"\\[CapitalPhi]\"}];\nMakeBoxes[sinPhi, TraditionalForm] := RowBox[{\"sin\", \"\\[ThinSpace]\", \"\\[CapitalPhi]\"}];\n\npdBox[num_, den_] := FractionBox[RowBox[{\"\\[PartialD]\", num}], RowBox[{\"\\[PartialD]\", den}]];\nMakeBoxes[daDalpha, TraditionalForm]  := pdBox[\"a\", \"\\[Alpha]\"];\nMakeBoxes[daDdelta, TraditionalForm]  := pdBox[\"a\", \"\\[Delta]\"];\nMakeBoxes[dbDalpha, TraditionalForm]  := pdBox[\"b\", \"\\[Alpha]\"];\nMakeBoxes[dbDdelta, TraditionalForm]  := pdBox[\"b\", \"\\[Delta]\"];\nMakeBoxes[dnrDalpha, TraditionalForm] := pdBox[RowBox[{\"(\", nrBox, \")\"}], \"\\[Alpha]\"];\nMakeBoxes[dnrDdelta, TraditionalForm] := pdBox[RowBox[{\"(\", nrBox, \")\"}], \"\\[Delta]\"];\n\n(* \"lhs = rhs\" table, and labels like dA21/diota *)\nparBox = <|h0 -> SubscriptBox[\"h\", \"0\"], iota -> \"\\[Iota]\", psi -> \"\\[Psi]\", phi0 -> SubscriptBox[\"\\[Phi]\", \"0\"],\n           f -> \"f\", fdot -> OverscriptBox[\"f\", \".\"], alpha -> \"\\[Alpha]\", delta -> \"\\[Delta]\"|>;\nlabels[name_, p_] := Table[DisplayForm[pdBox[SubscriptBox[name, \"2\" <> ToString[i]], parBox[p]]], {i, 4}];\nshow[lhs_, rhs_]  := TraditionalForm[Grid[Transpose[{lhs, ConstantArray[\"=\", Length[lhs]], rhs}], Alignment -> Left]];",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {},
   "executionSummary": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## Derivatives\n\nThe amplitude parameters enter only through $A_{2i}$ and the phase parameters only through the modes $h_{2i}$:\n\n$$\\frac{\\partial h}{\\partial \\theta_A} = \\sum_{i=1}^{4} \\frac{\\partial A_{2i}}{\\partial \\theta_A}\\,h_{2i},\\quad \\theta_A \\in \\{h_0,\\iota,\\psi,\\phi_0\\};\n\\qquad\n\\frac{\\partial h}{\\partial \\theta_\\Phi} = \\sum_{i=1}^{4} A_{2i}\\,\\frac{\\partial h_{2i}}{\\partial \\theta_\\Phi},\\quad \\theta_\\Phi \\in \\{f,\\dot f,\\alpha,\\delta\\}.$$\n\nSo the pieces needed are, in order:\n\n1. $\\partial A_{2i}/\\partial\\theta_A$\n2. $\\partial h_{2i}/\\partial\\theta_\\Phi$, which contain $\\partial a/\\partial\\alpha$, $\\partial b/\\partial\\alpha$, $\\partial(\\vec n\\cdot\\vec r)/\\partial\\alpha$ (and the same for $\\delta$)\n3. $\\partial a/\\partial\\alpha$, $\\partial a/\\partial\\delta$, $\\partial b/\\partial\\alpha$, $\\partial b/\\partial\\delta$\n4. $\\partial(\\vec n\\cdot\\vec r)/\\partial\\alpha$, $\\partial(\\vec n\\cdot\\vec r)/\\partial\\delta$",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {},
   "executionSummary": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### 1. Amplitude derivatives",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {},
   "executionSummary": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "dAmp = AssociationMap[D[Amp, #] &, ampPars];\n\nshow[labels[\"A\", h0], dAmp[h0]]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<div class=\"wexpr\"><wgraph class=\"resizable\" style=\"width:759px;height:184px;\" aspect-ratio=\"0.2424\" tabIndex=\"-1\"><img class=\"invert-brightness\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" /></wgraph></div>",
       "mime": "x-application/wolfram-language-html"
      }
     ],
     "id": "66ff7541-4b98-4ab6-a251-7bb9e4c20343"
    }
   ],
   "metadata": {},
   "executionSummary": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "show[labels[\"A\", iota], dAmp[iota]]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<div class=\"wexpr\"><wgraph class=\"resizable\" style=\"width:829px;height:168px;\" aspect-ratio=\"0.2027\" tabIndex=\"-1\"><img class=\"invert-brightness\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" /></wgraph></div>",
       "mime": "x-application/wolfram-language-html"
      }
     ],
     "id": "f3e30792-9455-4e20-af27-46e8ff1a2eec"
    }
   ],
   "metadata": {},
   "executionSummary": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "show[labels[\"A\", psi], dAmp[psi]]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<div class=\"wexpr\"><wgraph class=\"resizable\" style=\"width:836px;height:180px;\" aspect-ratio=\"0.2153\" tabIndex=\"-1\"><img class=\"invert-brightness\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" /></wgraph></div>",
       "mime": "x-application/wolfram-language-html"
      }
     ],
     "id": "f2527018-29be-4e3c-af1d-857bc81b08b0"
    }
   ],
   "metadata": {},
   "executionSummary": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "show[labels[\"A\", phi0], dAmp[phi0]]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<div class=\"wexpr\"><wgraph class=\"resizable\" style=\"width:814px;height:184px;\" aspect-ratio=\"0.2262\" tabIndex=\"-1\"><img class=\"invert-brightness\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" /></wgraph></div>",
       "mime": "x-application/wolfram-language-html"
      }
     ],
     "id": "80cbd447-fecc-4427-8ce0-0001f866684c"
    }
   ],
   "metadata": {},
   "executionSummary": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### 2. Mode derivatives",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {},
   "executionSummary": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "modeRules = {Derivative[1,0,0][a][alpha,delta,t]  -> daDalpha,  Derivative[0,1,0][a][alpha,delta,t]  -> daDdelta,\n             Derivative[1,0,0][b][alpha,delta,t]  -> dbDalpha,  Derivative[0,1,0][b][alpha,delta,t]  -> dbDdelta,\n             Derivative[1,0,0][nr][alpha,delta,t] -> dnrDalpha, Derivative[0,1,0][nr][alpha,delta,t] -> dnrDdelta,\n             aF -> a, bF -> b, nrF -> nr};\n\ndModes = AssociationMap[(D[modes, #] /. {Cos[Phi] -> cosPhi, Sin[Phi] -> sinPhi}) /. modeRules &, phasePars];\n\nshow[labels[\"h\", f], dModes[f]]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<div class=\"wexpr\"><wgraph class=\"resizable\" style=\"width:365px;height:191px;\" aspect-ratio=\"0.5241\" tabIndex=\"-1\"><img class=\"invert-brightness\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" /></wgraph></div>",
       "mime": "x-application/wolfram-language-html"
      }
     ],
     "id": "0984467d-5604-44c7-85d6-177fc899868b"
    }
   ],
   "metadata": {},
   "executionSummary": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "show[labels[\"h\", fdot], dModes[fdot]]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<div class=\"wexpr\"><wgraph class=\"resizable\" style=\"width:370px;height:194px;\" aspect-ratio=\"0.5260\" tabIndex=\"-1\"><img class=\"invert-brightness\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" /></wgraph></div>",
       "mime": "x-application/wolfram-language-html"
      }
     ],
     "id": "94571c07-a422-47d9-b96d-6478bcb3a1c3"
    }
   ],
   "metadata": {},
   "executionSummary": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "show[labels[\"h\", alpha], dModes[alpha]]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<div class=\"wexpr\"><wgraph class=\"resizable\" style=\"width:457px;height:255px;\" aspect-ratio=\"0.5587\" tabIndex=\"-1\"><img class=\"invert-brightness\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" /></wgraph></div>",
       "mime": "x-application/wolfram-language-html"
      }
     ],
     "id": "53c58825-936b-409a-9565-dd67c02e4cfb"
    }
   ],
   "metadata": {},
   "executionSummary": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "show[labels[\"h\", delta], dModes[delta]]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<div class=\"wexpr\"><wgraph class=\"resizable\" style=\"width:457px;height:257px;\" aspect-ratio=\"0.5622\" tabIndex=\"-1\"><img class=\"invert-brightness\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" /></wgraph></div>",
       "mime": "x-application/wolfram-language-html"
      }
     ],
     "id": "fa2a78c6-b8bc-49ac-91ca-a80905935048"
    }
   ],
   "metadata": {},
   "executionSummary": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### 3. Modulation function derivatives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\na(t) ={}& \\tfrac{1}{16}\\sin 2\\gamma\\,(3-\\cos 2\\lambda)(3-\\cos 2\\delta)\\cos 2x\n- \\tfrac{1}{4}\\cos 2\\gamma\\,\\sin\\lambda\\,(3-\\cos 2\\delta)\\sin 2x \\\\\n&+ \\tfrac{1}{4}\\sin 2\\gamma\\,\\sin 2\\lambda\\,\\sin 2\\delta\\,\\cos x\n- \\tfrac{1}{2}\\cos 2\\gamma\\,\\cos\\lambda\\,\\sin 2\\delta\\,\\sin x\n+ \\tfrac{3}{4}\\sin 2\\gamma\\,\\cos^2\\lambda\\,\\cos^2\\delta,\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nb(t) ={}& \\cos 2\\gamma\\,\\sin\\lambda\\,\\sin\\delta\\,\\cos 2x\n+ \\tfrac{1}{4}\\sin 2\\gamma\\,(3-\\cos 2\\lambda)\\sin\\delta\\,\\sin 2x \\\\\n&+ \\cos 2\\gamma\\,\\cos\\lambda\\,\\cos\\delta\\,\\cos x\n+ \\tfrac{1}{2}\\sin 2\\gamma\\,\\sin 2\\lambda\\,\\cos\\delta\\,\\sin x.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere $\\lambda$ is the detector latitude, $\\gamma$ the angle of the arm bisector measured counter-clockwise from East, and $x \\equiv \\alpha - \\phi_r - \\Omega_r t$ with $\\phi_r + \\Omega_r t$ the local sidereal time.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {},
   "executionSummary": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "xF = alpha - phir - OmegaR t;\n\naExpl = 1/16 Sin[2 gam] (3 - Cos[2 lambda]) (3 - Cos[2 delta]) Cos[2 xF] -\n        1/4  Cos[2 gam] Sin[lambda] (3 - Cos[2 delta]) Sin[2 xF] +\n        1/4  Sin[2 gam] Sin[2 lambda] Sin[2 delta] Cos[xF] -\n        1/2  Cos[2 gam] Cos[lambda] Sin[2 delta] Sin[xF] +\n        3/4  Sin[2 gam] Cos[lambda]^2 Cos[delta]^2;\n\nbExpl = Cos[2 gam] Sin[lambda] Sin[delta] Cos[2 xF] +\n        1/4 Sin[2 gam] (3 - Cos[2 lambda]) Sin[delta] Sin[2 xF] +\n        Cos[2 gam] Cos[lambda] Cos[delta] Cos[xF] +\n        1/2 Sin[2 gam] Sin[2 lambda] Cos[delta] Sin[xF];\n\nabDerivs = {D[aExpl, alpha], D[aExpl, delta], D[bExpl, alpha], D[bExpl, delta]} /. xF -> x;\n\nshow[DisplayForm /@ {pdBox[\"a\", \"\\[Alpha]\"], pdBox[\"a\", \"\\[Delta]\"], pdBox[\"b\", \"\\[Alpha]\"], pdBox[\"b\", \"\\[Delta]\"]}, abDerivs]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<div class=\"wexpr\"><wgraph class=\"resizable\" style=\"width:1717px;height:291px;\" aspect-ratio=\"0.1696\" tabIndex=\"-1\"><img class=\"invert-brightness\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" /></wgraph></div>",
       "mime": "x-application/wolfram-language-html"
      }
     ],
     "id": "7bde5d59-eb96-468a-8fad-fd4b247db6a6"
    }
   ],
   "metadata": {},
   "executionSummary": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### 4. Doppler term derivatives\n\nWith the ephemeris giving the detector position $\\vec r = (r_x, r_y, r_z)$ in equatorial (ICRS) coordinates in the SSB frame, the unit vector to the source is\n\n$$\\vec n = (\\cos\\alpha\\cos\\delta,\\ \\sin\\alpha\\cos\\delta,\\ \\sin\\delta),$$\n\nso\n\n$$\\vec n\\cdot\\vec r = r_x\\cos\\alpha\\cos\\delta + r_y\\sin\\alpha\\cos\\delta + r_z\\sin\\delta.$$\n\n$\\vec r$ is the Earth's position from the ephemeris plus the detector's position on the Earth, and depends only on $t$.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {},
   "executionSummary": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "nrExpl   = {Cos[alpha] Cos[delta], Sin[alpha] Cos[delta], Sin[delta]} . {rx, ry, rz};\nnrDerivs = {D[nrExpl, alpha], D[nrExpl, delta]};\n\nshow[DisplayForm /@ {pdBox[RowBox[{\"(\", nrBox, \")\"}], \"\\[Alpha]\"], pdBox[RowBox[{\"(\", nrBox, \")\"}], \"\\[Delta]\"]}, nrDerivs]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<div class=\"wexpr\"><wgraph class=\"resizable\" style=\"width:644px;height:93px;\" aspect-ratio=\"0.1441\" tabIndex=\"-1\"><img class=\"invert-brightness\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" /></wgraph></div>",
       "mime": "x-application/wolfram-language-html"
      }
     ],
     "id": "48552ba6-4e5d-4fd4-980b-054a6380ef35"
    }
   ],
   "metadata": {},
   "executionSummary": {}
  }
 ]
}